What the releases contain

  * PuyoPuyoTetris-Update-patched.cia: the game's update title (0004000E).
    Sega's own v1.2.0 update executable with the patched game data (the
    romfs) appended. It has the same shape as an official title update and,
    like one, launches only through a copy of the game you already own.
  * PuyoPuyoTetris-DLC-patched.cia: the 3DS DLC with English text, voices
    and icons substituted. Installable only alongside a copy of the game you
    already own.
  * PuyoPuyoTetris-LayeredFS.zip: only the files that changed, for Luma3DS
    game patching. Useless without the game.

What the releases do not contain

  * The Japanese base game (title 00040000), in any form. Not the CCI, not
    the CIA, not a patched copy, not its executable. A full patched base CIA
    can be built locally from your own dump with tools/build_cia.py, but it
    is not needed and is not distributed.
  * The Steam release or any file from it. The English text and voices were
    read from a legitimately purchased Steam copy on the author's machine and
    are present in the releases only as they were carried into the 3DS files.

The earlier fan translation this builds on is the work of its own authors;
the Adventure story text and the character-select textures in these builds
are theirs, unchanged.

Character names, mode names and other terminology follow Sega's official
English localisation wherever it exists.
